# Overrides for the one directory that talks directly to kernel APIs.
#
# The BSD sockets interface is defined in terms of `struct sockaddr*`, and the
# only way to pass a `sockaddr_un` to bind()/connect() is a reinterpret_cast.
# There is no conforming alternative -- static_cast will not do it, and a union
# would merely hide the same cast behind more code. Week 5 adds sockaddr_can
# for SocketCAN, which has exactly the same shape.
#
# The check stays enabled everywhere else, where a reinterpret_cast really is
# a smell worth arguing about.

InheritParentConfig: true

Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast
